  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1, vocal line, verified against the LilyPond score on Italian Wikipedia (written with German note names, so h = B and b = B♭). The first section is sung once (its repeat carries verse 2); the second section is played twice with the first and then the second ending, as the score's own playback unfolds it. Slurred notes carry one syllable over two notes ('Santa Lucia' on the eighth-note pairs). Simplification: two chromatic E naturals (passing note on 'l'onda' and lower neighbour on 'mia') are played as 4 (E♭). D drum: as written (range 2 to high 3), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2/3, so 'Venite all'agile barchetta' (both times), the first three notes of each 'Santa Lucia,' line, and everything from the last two notes of that line to the end of the following 'Santa Lucia!' are played one octave lower (the middle notes 5 5 3 4 stay at pitch); C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
